        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): route llama.cpp GBNF cleaning through provider tool-schema hooks",
        "body": "Fixes #108367\nFixes #108473\nFixes #108580\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen OpenClaw runs against a llama.cpp-backed endpoint with grammar-constrained tool calling, chat requests fail with HTTP 400 before inference whenever the active tool list includes GBNF-hostile JSON Schema constructs (#108580):\n\n1. Unanchored / PCRE-shorthand `pattern` (e.g. `\\\\S`)\n2. `maxLength` above llama.cpp's ~2000 GBNF repetition ceiling (e.g. cron `trigger.script` `65536`)\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nCanonical tool schemas keep their server-side validation guidance. Cleaning happens only on llama.cpp-compatible routes:\n\n| Activation path | Who owns it |\n|---|---|\n| Bundled `ollama`, `ollama-cloud`, `lmstudio`, `llama-cpp` | Provider-owned `normalizeToolSchemas` via `buildProviderToolCompatFamilyHooks(\"llamacpp-gbnf\")` |\n| Custom OpenAI-compatible llama.cpp endpoints | Opt-in `modelCompat.toolSchemaProfile: \"llamacpp\"` |\n| Ordinary providers (`openai`, etc.) | Unchanged — canonical `pattern` / `maxLength` retained |\n\nShared-core provider-ID guessing was removed (ClawSweeper P1). This mirrors the Gemini family-helper pattern in `openclaw/plugin-sdk/provider-tools`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nllama.cpp / Ollama / LM Studio users can keep cron and related tools enabled without pre-inference grammar 400s. OpenAI and other providers keep model-facing length/pattern constraints.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Exact-head bundled-provider live proof (head `71f51dbe274`)\n\nThis run registered the real bundled Ollama plugin, selected its provider-owned `normalizeToolSchemas` hook, printed the outbound schema, and sent that schema to a local `llama-server` b9960. Private endpoint details are omitted.\n\n```text\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/ollama/exact-head-gbnf-live-proof.test.ts --reporter=verbose\nEXACT_HEAD=71f51dbe274\nPROVIDER_HOOK=ollama\nOUTBOUND_SCHEMA={\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"declarationKey\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"minLength\":1,\"maxLength\":200},\"script\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"minLength\":1}}}\nLLAMA_SERVER_HTTP=200\nINFERENCE_RESPONSE={\"choices\":[{\"finish_reason\":\"stop\",\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"ready\"}}],...}\n\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests       1 passed (1)\n```\n\nThis proves the current bundled-provider activation path: `pattern` and oversized `maxLength: 65536` are absent from the outbound schema, `maxLength: 200` remains, and llama-server successfully reaches inference.\n\n### Public contract documentation\n\nThe custom-endpoint profile and provider SDK family are documented as supported contracts:\n\n- `docs/gateway/local-models.md`: `compat.toolSchemaProfile: \"llamacpp\"`, affected bundled providers, exact cleaning behavior, and ordinary-provider preservation\n- `docs/plugins/sdk-provider-plugins.md`: `llamacpp-gbnf` family behavior and bundled examples\n- `docs/plugins/sdk-subpaths.md` / `docs/plugins/sdk-migration.md`: public `provider-tools` surface inventory\n- `docs/.generated/plugin-sdk-api-baseline.sha256`: regenerated API contract manifest\n\n### Focused tests\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs \\\n  packages/ai/src/providers/clean-for-llamacpp-gbnf.test.ts \\\n  packages/ai/src/providers/agent-tools-parameter-schema.llamacpp.test.ts \\\n  src/plugin-sdk/provider-tools.test.ts \\\n  src/agents/tools/tool-schema-llamacpp-compat.test.ts \\\n  extensions/ollama/index.test.ts \\\n  extensions/lmstudio/index.test.ts \\\n  extensions/llama-cpp/index.test.ts\n```\nAll green on Node 22.\n\n### Live llama-server regression transcript (shipped failure)\nEarlier local `llama-server` b9960 run against the shipped grammar-hostile cron schema:\n\n- unanchored `\\\\S` → HTTP 400 `Pattern must start with '^' and end with '$'`\n- `maxLength: 65536` → HTTP 400 `failed to parse grammar`\n- cleaned schema (same projection the provider hook now emits) → HTTP 200, inference proceeds\n\nThe cleaned payload that reached HTTP 200 is exactly what `normalizeLlamacppGbnfToolSchemas` / `toolSchemaProfile: \"llamacpp\"` emit on this head.\n\n### vs #108671\n#108671 removes constraints from canonical tool schemas globally. This PR preserves them and cleans only on llama.cpp-compatible provider/profile routes — the ownership ClawSweeper recommended.\n",
        "branch": "fix/cron-schema-anchored-patterns",
